    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Property Summary\r\nA rare opportunity to acquire a stunning turnkey duplex apartment in the heart of Castlebridge village, beautifully positioned within the historic Old Mill and enjoying wonderful views across the village and towards the coast.  The Old Mill brings a unique character and sense of history to the property.  The building retains its original mill wheel, a charming reminder of its former industrial heritage, while the apartments provide modern and\r\ncomfortable living. Ideally located within walking distance of Castlebridge's welcoming coffee shops, local shops and characterful antique and furniture stores, the property offers the convenience of village living with the coast and countryside close at hand. Wexford Town is easily accessible, while the beautiful Curracloe Beach and Raven Point are also nearby. Apartment 11 is a spacious two-bedroom duplex extending over the second and third floors, presented in turnkey condition and designed to make the most of its elevated position and attractive surroundings. A particular highlight is the bright open-plan kitchen/dining/living area, which opens onto a balcony enjoying a sunny aspect and wonderful views across the village and towards the coast.  The accommodation is thoughtfully arranged over two floors, offering a bright and comfortable layout with excellent views. The second floor features a welcoming entrance hall, a well-proportioned second bedroom and a generous open-plan kitchen/dining/living area, with the living space opening onto a private balcony enjoying a sunny aspect and wonderful views across the village and towards the coast. The third floor provides a spacious master bedroom with Velux windows and attractive views, together with a private ensuite. A separate family bathroom, generous landing, storage and access to the attic space complete the accommodation. Extending to approximately 90.97 sq. m. (c. 979 sq. ft.), the apartment offers well-balanced living space with the added appeal of its elevated duplex layout and distinctive village and coastal outlook.  VIEWING HIGHLY RECOMMENDED."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Property Accommodation\r\n\r\nEntrance Hall - (3.31m x 1.97m), Laminate floor, hotpress off, intercom.\r\nBedroom 2 - (3.24m x 2.96m), Carpeted.\r\nKitchen/Dining/Living Area - (6.10m x 4.92m), Kitchen - Eye & waist level kitchen units, oven, hob & extractor fan, tiled flooring & splashback.\r\nDining/Living area – Laminate floor, door to balcony with fabulous views including sea views and ideally positioned with sunny aspect.\r\nFIRST FLOOR\r\nLanding - (4.35m x 3.00m), Carpeted, access to attic space, storage press off, exit door to fire escape.\r\nMaster Bedroom - (6.23m x 2.96m), Carpeted, velux windows with views.\r\nEnsuite - (2.22m x 1.03m),  Tiled floor, WC, WHB & Triton Shower.\r\nBathroom- (3.37m x 1.82m), Tiled floor, WC, WHB, bath with shower head over, tiled around bath.\r\n\r\nOutside : 1 designated car parking space, ample parking spaces for visitors.\r\nServices: Electricity, mains water, mains sewerage, electric storage heating.\r\nBER: C Ber No: 106910649 Performance indicator: 161.63 Wh/m2/yr"
